yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Multi-agent worktrees
.worktrees/

# Finder / file-sync duplicates. A sync client on at least one dev machine creates
# "name 2.ts" copies of every file during a large checkout. They are untracked, but the
# vitest globs match them, so a polluted working tree produces a red suite that has
# nothing to do with the code. Ignore them so `git status` stays readable; delete them
# with:  git clean -n '* 2.*'   then   git clean -f '* 2.*'
* 2.*
* 2
